Deferred commits in the background: a commit the embedder holds back keeps its command buffer uncommitted in its
queue's FIFO and returns at once, instead of waiting in patch 0003's gate (Minato, patch 0025).

Why: iOS refuses a command buffer committed after the app moved to the background (MTLCommandBufferErrorNotPermitted),
so patch 0003's gate held every commit there until the foreground, with the committing thread inside. An app thread
that also reads the app's events then never reached its pause: a Ren'Py game's texture uploads on SDL's surfaceless
context parked its main thread for the whole background, and its save on pause ran only at the return. Encoding is
CPU work; only the commit is refused. Now ANGLEMetalSetCommitDeferral(enter, waitForeground) replaces the gate's wait:
enter() answers whether a commit may go (counted as 0003's gate counts it, until its second function), and a commit
held back goes into the queue's FIFO. The FIFO is committed in order before the next commit enter() lets go, so the
queue's order is kept: a wait until scheduled of a deferred command buffer (the flush in eglMakeCurrent's unbind) has
nothing to wait for. Only a wait for a result waits for the foreground and then commits the FIFO: glFinish and every
WaitUntilFinished flush (queries, buffer reads, readPixels), a CPU access to a resource (ensureResourceReadyForCPU, the
buffer pool's reuse) and a client wait without an end; a bounded client wait waits its time. A full FIFO, 32 command
buffers (Metal's queue hands out 64 that are not completed, an uncommitted one included) or 512 MiB of their
resources, makes the next commit wait for the foreground as 0003 did. Without the deferral set, 0003's gate is
unchanged. ANGLEMetalDeferredCounters gives the FIFOs' numbers, and ANGLEMetalParkingLine appends " defer=<n>
dbytes=<MiB> dpeak=<MiB> dtotal=<n> dfull=<n>". A command buffer still deferred when its queue is torn down is
dropped.
Test: graphics/tests/angle_commit_defer.mm (an upload, a clear, glFlush and the unbind return at once in the
background with nothing committed; glFinish waits for the foreground and the texture then holds the background's
work; the 33rd command buffer waits for the foreground and is counted), graphics/tests/gles_gate_test.c through
graphics/host. graphics/host/background_commit_probe.m checks on the iPhone that encoding in the background and
committing at the foreground is allowed.
Upstream: no; it serves one embedder's lifecycle.
Remove: not while Minato keeps apps off the GPU in the background.

